  "instance_name": "racial_stereotyping",
  "label": "Racial Stereotyping",
  "description": "The meme relies on the broader concept of racial stereotyping — the oversimplified and often negative assumptions about a racial group. In this case, it stereotypes Black people as being 'out of place' or 'inappropriate' for celebrating American holidays, which is a form of racial exclusion and can be seen as a microaggression or hate speech. This stereotype is rooted in historical racism and continues to be used to marginalize Black Americans.",
